ralph/progress.txt:19364:The 20-test shape pins: Append-mints-id-and-row-shape (depev_ prefix), Append-blank-fields-default (Message='' RequestID='' CorrelationID='' Metadata=nil), Append-respects-caller-supplied-id, Append-respects-caller-supplied-occurred-at (worker-reconciliation contract), Append-unknown-event-type-rejected (CHECK via mapWriteError -> Conflict), Append-blank-event-type-rejected (apierr.Internal at application boundary, NOT a database-CHECK pass-through — the empty string is a programming error caught before SQL, since a blank value would also pass the CHECK if the CHECK accepted '' which it does not but the application boundary catches it first), Append-unknown-deployment-rejected (composite FK -> Conflict), Append-cross-tenant-deployment-rejected (composite FK -> Conflict + countDeploymentEventRowsForDeployment proves no row persisted), Append-duplicate-id-Conflict (PRIMARY KEY collision via mapWriteError), Append-nil-Tx-Internal, Append-rolls-back-on-tx-rollback, Append-peer-row-byte-identity (NO updated_at column to drift, so the test asserts byte-identity on id+EventType+Message+OccurredAt+CreatedAt — the absence of bump_version + set_updated_at triggers MEANS the peer can never drift on a successful sibling Append), Update-rejected-by-trigger (raw `db.Exec UPDATE` bypasses the repository surface entirely so the trigger is the only thing that can stop the write), cascade-delete-on-deployment (raw `DELETE FROM deployments WHERE id = $1` cascades through the composite FK ON DELETE CASCADE), GetByID-returns-persisted-row / unknown-NotFound / cross-tenant-NotFound-with-no-leak-on-foreign-deployment-id, ListByDeployment-chronological-order (seed three rows OUT OF chronological order so the ASC ordering must reorder them on read), ListByDeployment-unknown-deployment-empty (returns empty slice not error — distinguishes "no events" from "no parent" is the caller's responsibility, mirrors deployment ListByService), ListByDeployment-cross-tenant-empty. The peer-row test gets simpler than quota_reservations or deployments because there is NO updated_at column to drift and NO version column to bump — append-only is structural in the column list, not just the trigger. Forward-applicable to every future append-only event-log surface (e.g. provisioning_job_events when that lands).
ralph/progress.txt:19366:GOTCHA on apierr.Internal for blank-event-type at the application boundary (NOT mapWriteError -> Conflict): a blank EventType `""` would pass the `event_type IN (...)` CHECK only if `''` were in the closed set, which it is not — but the test must still encode that the application boundary catches it FIRST and surfaces yerr.CodeInternal, not the database CHECK surfacing yerr.CodeConflict. The repository explicitly does `if e.EventType == "" { return apierr.Internal(...) }` before any SQL — same reason AuditRepository.Append explicitly checks `if !e.Decision.Valid()` rather than letting the database CHECK reject it. The constraint surface and the application-boundary surface have DIFFERENT typed errors, and the test must pin both.
ralph/progress.txt:19368:GOTCHA on the apierr import being unused in the test file: yerr.From().Code is how the test reaches typed codes; the test never directly constructs an apierr. Don't add a placeholder `var _ = apierr.Internal` to keep the import — just omit the apierr import entirely. The auto-import-cleanup pass (when goimports runs) catches this anyway, but writing the file correctly the first time avoids a wasted edit cycle.
