ralph/progress.txt:31593:- Tests prove: Upsert INSERT branch returns the committed row (version=1, timestamps non-zero + byte-equal on fresh row, fields echoed verbatim, env/svc pointer round-trip); Upsert UPDATE branch on the scope-tuple conflict only mutates role + bumps version + refreshes updated_at + preserves created_at + ignores the caller-supplied id + keeps the existing principal_kind (cross-kind smuggling impossible); Upsert cross-tenant or unknown project_id surfaces typed apierr.Conflict via the composite FK to projects; Upsert duplicate primary-key id surfaces typed apierr.Conflict; DeleteByProjectExceptIDs with nil OR empty keepIDs clears all rows of (org, project) AND treats both forms identically; DeleteByProjectExceptIDs with keepIDs retains only the listed rows; DeleteByProjectExceptIDs is tenant-scoped (cross-tenant projectID cannot reach into another org's grants); ON DELETE CASCADE from projects removes grants when the parent project is hard-deleted; Upsert rolls back when the surrounding Write closure returns a non-nil error (proved via ListByProject — the only observation surface for a grant row); Upsert and DeleteByProjectExceptIDs nil-Tx guards render typed apierr.Internal, never a nil-pointer panic.
ralph/progress.txt:31659:- Tests prove: Insert returns row at version=1 with database-assigned, byte-equal CreatedAt/UpdatedAt (no UPDATE trigger has fired yet) and DeletionScheduledAt=nil; round-trip GetByID returns the same row; Update bumps version by exactly +1, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves Kind / OrganizationID / ProjectID (the SET clause must touch slug/display_name only), and leaves DeletionScheduledAt nil on a live row; Update with matching If-Match succeeds (positive companion to the stale-If-Match conflict path already in environment_update_test.go); ScheduleDeletion bumps version by exactly +1, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves identity fields (slug, display_name, kind) and the composite (organization_id, project_id) tenant key, and stamps DeletionScheduledAt at-or-after baseline.UpdatedAt; Insert inside a Write closure that returns a sentinel error rolls back — GetByID surfaces typed NotFound and ListByProject does not see the rolled-back row, so a half-written environment cannot survive an aborted audit/policy/quota step alongside it; Insert with a nil *store.Tx renders a typed apierr.Internal (the matrix-closer for env's nil-Tx guard coverage — Update and ScheduleDeletion nil-Tx guards already covered in environment_update_test.go and environment_delete_test.go).
ralph/progress.txt:31700:- Tests prove: (a) Upsert INSERT branch returns the committed row with version=1, byte-equal CreatedAt/UpdatedAt (no UPDATE trigger has fired yet), all caller-supplied fields echoed verbatim, nil ServiceID stays nil; (b) Upsert INSERT with non-nil service_id round-trips the pointer to the exact text and accepts principal_kind="sa" alongside "usr"; (c) Upsert UPDATE branch on the scope-tuple conflict mutates ONLY role, bumps version via the environment_grants_bump_version trigger, refreshes updated_at via the environment_grants_set_updated_at trigger, preserves created_at, IGNORES the caller-supplied id (persisted id stays at baseline's id), preserves principal_kind (cross-kind smuggling impossible — the caller's "sa" does not stick when baseline is "usr"), and preserves the immutable identifiers (organization_id, environment_id, principal_id, service_id); (d) Upsert with cross-tenant environment_id surfaces typed apierr.Conflict via the MATCH SIMPLE composite FK (organization_id, environment_id) -> environments; (e) Upsert with unknown environment_id under the caller's tenant lands on the same typed Conflict for the same FK reason; (f) Upsert with duplicate primary key (different principal_id so the scope-tuple ON CONFLICT branch does NOT match) surfaces typed Conflict via the PRIMARY KEY (id) constraint; (g) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with nil keepIDs clears all grants of (org, env); (h) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with empty-slice keepIDs is identical to nil; (i) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with a non-empty keepIDs keeps exactly the listed ids and drops every other row; (j) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs is tenant-scoped — a cross-tenant environmentID under the caller's organization_id matches zero rows, leaving the other tenant's bystander grant byte-untouched and the caller's own grant intact; (k) ON DELETE CASCADE from environments removes every environment_grants row when the parent environments row is deleted directly (NOT via ScheduleDeletion which is a soft delete); (l) Upsert rolls back when the surrounding Write closure returns a non-nil error — the row does not surface at ListByEnvironment outside the rolled-back transaction (the only observation surface for grants); (m) nil-Tx guards on Upsert AND DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs render typed apierr.Internal — never a nil-pointer panic.
ralph/progress.txt:31752:- Tests prove: (a) Insert returns the committed row with version=1, byte-equal CreatedAt/UpdatedAt (no UPDATE trigger has fired yet), nil DeletionScheduledAt, and round-trips identity (id/org/project/env/slug/name/kind) plus GetByID re-read agrees; (b) Update bumps version by exactly +1 via services_bump_version, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves Kind (the SET clause must touch slug/display_name only — Kind is immutable Dokploy taxonomy enforced by the migration-0002 CHECK), preserves the composite (organization_id, project_id, environment_id) tenant key (Update is a PATCH, not a re-parenting), and leaves DeletionScheduledAt nil on a live row; (c) Update with matching If-Match succeeds (positive companion to the stale-If-Match conflict path through classifyServiceConcurrencyMiss); (d) ScheduleDeletion bumps version, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves identity (slug/display_name/kind), preserves the composite tenant key, and stamps deletion_scheduled_at at or after baseline.UpdatedAt; (e) Restore is the inverse projected through the same dual-anchor — bumps version, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves identity and the composite tenant key, and clears deletion_scheduled_at back to NULL (the load-bearing assertion since a missing `SET deletion_scheduled_at = NULL` would still trip the version/updated_at anchors); (f) Insert participates in the surrounding transaction as the unit of work — a closure error rolls the row back so GetByID surfaces NotFound AND ListByEnvironment does not see it; (g/h/i) nil-Tx guards on Insert, Update, and ScheduleDeletion render typed apierr.Internal — never a nil-pointer panic (Restore's nil-Tx guard is already covered by TestServiceRepositoryRestoreRejectsNilTx in service_restore_test.go).
ralph/progress.txt:32441:  - **The application-boundary error class for "the application caught this before the database had a chance" is apierr.Internal, not apierr.InvalidInput.** A blank EventType at the repository's Append surface is a programming error (the application should never send it; the closed set is a Go type) — the typed code is yerr.CodeInternal. apierr.InvalidInput is reserved for the HTTP/service layer where the customer's request is being validated; a repository call site has no customer-facing context. Same pattern as AuditRepository.Append rejecting an invalid Decision with Internal.
